# Mains-frequency flicker seen by the AS7343's flicker ADC. Minted because the
# standard set carries no flicker type (ADR-0005 d2).
#
# Flags, not a measurement -- the device reports detection at two fixed
# frequencies and nothing about depth or phase. The profile's fixture is DC
# driven (M02 spec 3), so an asserted flag is a driver fault indication rather
# than an ambient property.
#
# Detected and valid are separate fields on purpose: the device computes the two
# frequencies independently and can complete a measurement in which neither
# calculation converged. `detected_*` is meaningless where the matching
# `*_valid` is false, which a single tri-state per frequency would have hidden
# behind an encoding every consumer would decode differently.
#
# Report only. Like door and leak (ADR-0005 d4), this type carries no command
# and no actuation contract: the response to a flickering fixture is a
# gateway-side decision, and M02 switches nothing.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
bool valid              # the flicker measurement completed this cycle
bool saturation         # the flicker ADC saturated; the result may not hold
bool valid_100hz        # the 100 Hz calculation converged
bool valid_120hz        # the 120 Hz calculation converged
bool detected_100hz
bool detected_120hz
@extent 16 * 8
